@startuml

<style>
.OS {
    LineThickness 5.0
}
</style>

skinparam sequenceArrowColor Black
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor White
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor Black
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor Black
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor DarkGray
skinparam sequenceGroupBodyBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor LightYellow
skinparam NoteBorderColor Gray
skinparam NoteTextAlignment left
skinparam ParticipantFontName Courier
skinparam sequenceFontName Courier
skinparam ArrowFontName Courier

title Server <-> Client Sequence Diagram: Underlying-Layer (OS/Transport) Faults (Linux: Unix Domain Sockets)

participant "ExternalClient" as ExternalClient
participant "ClientConnection" as client_connection
participant "UnixDomainEngine" as unix_domain_engine
participant "UnixDomainServer" as unix_domain_server
participant "ExternalServer" as ExternalServer

note across : Companion to server_client_sequence_linux.puml (happy path) and\nserver_client_internal_fault_sequence.puml (library-internal resource limits).\nThis diagram covers faults originating in the OS/transport layer that the\nlibrary detects and reports, but does not itself cause or prevent -\ni.e. non-happy paths of the underlying layers, not user contract misuse\nand not library-internal bookkeeping limits.\nThe QNX Dispatch counterpart is server_client_os_fault_sequence_qnx.puml.

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== Connection Refused: Insufficient Permissions (StopReason::kPermission) ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

ExternalClient -> client_connection : (Start(\n  state_callback,\n  notify_callback\n))
note over client_connection : Invokes state_callback(kStarting)
client_connection -> unix_domain_engine : TryOpenClientConnection(identifier)
note over unix_domain_engine : Returns score::os::Error (EACCES-equivalent)
note over client_connection : Invokes state_callback(kStopping),\nthen state_callback(kStopped)
note left : GetStopReason() == StopReason::kPermission\nPer i_client_connection.h: "highly unlikely to\nhave a successful Restart()" for this reason

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== Server Bind/Startup Failure ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

ExternalServer -> unix_domain_server : (StartListening(...))
note over unix_domain_server : Returns score::cpp::expected_blank<Error> (error)
note right : IServer::StartListening() returning an error is\nthe only signal; the server never starts accepting\nconnections. Grounds the previously un-evidenced FTA\nbasic events "Duplicate Server Name" and "Server\nfactory queue size configured below the required\nminimum" (fta_ipc_channel_unavailable.puml, IE_Startup).

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== Peer Crash / Unexpected Disconnect While Ready (StopReason::kClosedByPeer) ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

note over client_connection, unix_domain_server : Setup and connection establishment already completed as in\nserver_client_sequence_linux.puml (omitted here for brevity); both\nendpoints are in their Ready-equivalent state.

note over unix_domain_server : (server process crashes / exits)
client_connection -> unix_domain_engine : ReceiveProtocolMessage(fd, code)
note over unix_domain_engine : => peer closed / broken pipe detected
note over client_connection : Invokes state_callback(kStopping),\nthen state_callback(kStopped)
note left : GetStopReason() == StopReason::kClosedByPeer

note over unix_domain_server : Detected independently on the server side once the OS reports\nthe peer gone; invokes DisconnectCallback(connection) or\nIConnectionHandler::OnDisconnect(connection)

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== Communication Error Prevents Continuation (StopReason::kIoError) ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

ExternalClient -> client_connection : (Send(message) / SendWaitReply(...) / SendWithCallback(...))
client_connection -> unix_domain_engine : SendProtocolMessage(fd, code, message)
note over unix_domain_engine : Returns score::os::Error\n(e.g. corrupted framing, unexpected errno)
note over client_connection : Invokes state_callback(kStopping),\nthen state_callback(kStopped)
note left : GetStopReason() == StopReason::kIoError

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== SendWithCallback: Reply Lost Because Peer Disconnects Mid-Flight ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

ExternalClient -> client_connection : (SendWithCallback(message, reply_callback))
client_connection -> unix_domain_engine : SendProtocolMessage(fd, code, message)
note over unix_domain_engine : Delivers the message over the connected socket
note over unix_domain_server : Invokes IConnectionHandler::OnMessageSentWithReply(\n  connection, message\n)
note over unix_domain_server : (server disconnects/crashes\nbefore calling Reply())
note over client_connection : Invokes reply_callback(error)
note left : Per i_client_connection.h: "if the server receives\nthe message but dies or disconnects before the reply\narrives to the client, the error will be passed to\nthe callback; the method itself will not return\nan error."

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== System-Wide Memory Exhaustion (ENOMEM) ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

ExternalClient -> client_connection : (Start(...) / Send(...))
client_connection -> unix_domain_engine : TryOpenClientConnection(identifier)
note over unix_domain_engine : Or SendProtocolMessage(); returns ENOMEM (system memory\nallocation limit reached)
note left : Per client-server.md: "We don't expect to be able to\npreallocate all the needed system memory resources.\nWe rely on ENOMEM error for handling of system memory\nallocation limits on QNX." Not preventable by the\nlibrary; reported the same way as other transport\nerrors (kIoError or a Send()/SendWaitReply() error).

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== Server-Side Incoming Backpressure Delegated to the OS ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

ExternalClient -> client_connection : (Send(message) [rapid, repeated])
client_connection -> unix_domain_engine : SendProtocolMessage(fd, code, message)
note over unix_domain_server : Today, UnixDomainServer does not implement\nServerConfig::max_queued_sends as an internal ring buffer\n(see memory_and_size_limits_findings.md, finding 4).\nBackpressure for incoming Send/REQUEST messages is delegated\nentirely to the OS socket buffer, not to library-managed\nqueueing. If that OS-level buffer is full,\nSendProtocolMessage() itself blocks or fails (EAGAIN-equivalent)\nbefore the message is considered sent by the library - i.e. this\nis an OS-layer fault, not the library-internal, deterministic\nrejection shown for max_queued_sends/max_async_replies in\nserver_client_internal_fault_sequence.puml.

@enduml
